  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Laela Maize Capacity Building Project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The USADF grant of $92,044 being sought by Laela AMCOS will enhance the capacity of the AMCOS to improve the financial and agricultural practices and capacity of the members to increase maize production productivity as well as secure assured markets for farmers maize. Through technical assistance, the capacity of the farmers and the AMCOS as their will be the focal point for economic emancipation will be enhanced to have a strong bargaining position and competitiveness in the maize business..A total of more than 200 AMCOS members and beneficiaries associated with the AMCOS will be impacted through better farming prices, post harvest handling of maize produce to minimize losses and more importantly will have an assured market for their maize produce at pre-agreed and competitive prices. Through their collective effort the farmers will have a stronger voice while negotiating with buyers as a well as dialogue with government for a conducive business environment. On their part, the AMCOS members will contribute and enhance their skills in maize farming on their more than 3,000 acres of land they own (individual plots that add up to 3,025 acres). They will also adopt better skills in maize production and productivity while minimizing post harvest losses.</narrative>
  </description>
